    "memoText": " \n                         VETO MESSAGE - No. 136\n \nTO THE SENATE:\n \nI am returning herewith, without my approval, the following bill:\n \nSenate Bill Number 4862, entitled:\n \n    \"AN  ACT  to  amend the insurance law, in relation to establishing a\n      captive insurance program for commuter  vans;  and  to  amend  the\n      state  finance  law,  in relation to establishing the commuter van\n      trust fund\"\n \n    NOT APPROVED\n \n  This bill would reallocate funds currently  committed  to  the  Empire\nState Development Corporation's Commuter Van Stabilization Pilot Program\n(the \"Pilot Program\") to a newly created Commuter Van Trust Fund.\n \n  The  Pilot  Program  was created to assist commuter van operators with\ninsurance subsidies to help address challenges in  obtaining  affordable\ncoverage.  Taking  funding away from the Pilot Program, which was estab-\nlished in the fiscal year 2022-23 budget and was also aimed  at  offset-\nting  insurance  costs  for the industry, would not be prudent. The bill\nalso has several technical issues that would make implementation  highly\nchallenging and legally questionable.\n \n  Therefore, I am constrained to veto this bill.\n \n  The bill is disapproved.                       (signed) KATHY HOCHUL\n \n                               __________\n",
    "signedDate": null,
    "signer": "KATHY HOCHUL",
